<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 625 mln stg further help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 625 mln stg further help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with a further 625 million stg of assistance at established interest rates.</p>
<p>The Bank allotted 125 million stg outright in bills and 500 million stg in repos to July 16 and 17.</p>
<p>It has now provided liquidity totalling 925 million pounds on Thursday in response to a forecast money market shortage of 1.2 billion stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
</text>
